  "articleBody": "Before you even think about putting up drywall in your basement, it is absolutely crucial to address any moisture problems. Skipping this step is one of the most frequent and costly mistakes homeowners make, leading to bigger headaches down the road. Hidden leaks, condensation, or mold are far easier to fix *before* you enclose the ceiling with drywall.\n\nStart by inspecting for any signs of water intrusion or dampness. Check your foundation walls, pipes, and around windows for any leaks or stains. Make sure your basement is well-ventilated to prevent condensation build-up, and consider running a dehumidifier if humidity is consistently high. If you find any active leaks or persistent dampness, get them repaired by a professional. This might involve exterior drainage solutions or interior sealing, depending on the cause. Installing moisture-resistant drywall can offer an extra layer of protection, but it's not a substitute for solving the root cause of the moisture. Taking the time to properly waterproof and mitigate moisture now will save you from potential mold growth, structural damage, and the need for costly drywall replacement in the future. If you're uncertain about the extent of your moisture issues or the best way to address them, HH Remodeling LLC can assess your basement and help ensure it's ready for a successful drywall installation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
